{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RandomizedSVD"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Computes an approximate rank-k SVD of an M×N matrix A:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A ≈ U * diag(S) * Vᵀ"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"where U is M×k orthonormal, S is k-vector of singular values, Vᵀ is k×N."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Complexity","level":2,"anchor":"Complexity","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Range sketch + power iterations + projection run in (O(M \\cdot N \\cdot l \\cdot (q + 1))) floating-point work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(with QR on an (M \\times l) sketch and exact SVD on an (l \\times N) core matrix, where (l = \\min(\\min(M, N), k + p))),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dramatically faster than full "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dgesdd_"},{"type":"text","text":" (O(M \\cdot N \\cdot \\min(M, N))) when (k \\ll \\min(M, N))."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Algorithm (Halko 2011)","level":2,"anchor":"Algorithm-Halko-2011","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Draw random Gaussian matrix (\\Omega \\in \\mathbb{R}^{N \\times l}) where (l = \\min(\\min(M, N), k + p))."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compute range sketch (Y = A \\cdot \\Omega) via BLAS "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dgemm"},{"type":"text","text":" with (q) subspace power iterations."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Orthonormalize (Y) via thin QR ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dgeqrf"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dorgqr"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Project (B = Q^T \\cdot A) (small (l \\times N) matrix)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compute small exact SVD of (B) with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dgesdd_"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Back-project left singular vectors: (U = Q \\cdot \\tilde{U}).","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Accuracy","text":"Accuracy"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Probabilistic error follows Halko, Martinsson, & Tropp (2011) bounds governed by singular-value decay,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oversampling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nOversamples"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":"), and power iterations ","type":"text"},{"code":"nPowerIter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); this is not an unconditional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deterministic (1 + \\varepsilon) guarantee for flat or slow-decay spectra.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reference","level":2,"anchor":"Reference","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Halko N., Martinsson P.G., Tropp J.A. (2011). Finding Structure with Randomness:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Probabilistic Algorithms for Constructing Approximate Matrix Decompositions."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SIAM Review 53(2):217–288."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Randomized Singular Value Decomposition using the Halko et al. (2011) algorithm.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/Swi